## 4. Skill workflow (agent / human)

### Step 0 — Read LOCK + current page

```bash
# Dev hosts
pnpm --filter @apps/marketing run dev
# http://denali.localhost:3002/  http://urban.localhost:3002/
```

Read: MASTER.md · home.md · marketing-landing.mdoc §4 (sections) · open `/` at **375px** width.

### Step 1 — Design system (required, once per PR-4 kickoff)

```bash
cd /path/to/app-tour
python3 .cursor/skills/ui-ux-pro-max/scripts/search.py \
  "mountain hiking club outdoor tour landing mobile trustworthy cinematic premium" \
  --design-system -p "Denali Club" -f markdown
```

**Save output** to `docs/workspaces/denali/appendices/cp-skill-denali-landing-YYYY-MM-DD.md` (decision log).

### Step 2 — Domain deep-dives (pick 2–4, not all)

```bash
# Landing structure — prefer Hero + social-proof patterns
python3 .cursor/skills/ui-ux-pro-max/scripts/search.py \
  "hero social-proof tour cards mobile scroll trust" \
  --domain landing -n 5

# Mobile UX
python3 .cursor/skills/ui-ux-pro-max/scripts/search.py \
  "mobile-first touch targets reduced-motion scroll-snap" \
  --domain ux -n 8

# Visual effects (keywords only — not colors)
python3 .cursor/skills/ui-ux-pro-max/scripts/search.py \
  "cinematic hero gradient overlay photography" \
  --domain style -n 5

# Optional: prompt domain for CSS vocabulary
python3 .cursor/skills/ui-ux-pro-max/scripts/search.py \
  "premium outdoor adventure landing" \
  --domain prompt -n 3
```

**Do not** run `--persist` into `design-system/MASTER.md` — Denali MASTER already exists; skill persist would **overwrite** brand tokens.

### Step 3 — Map skill patterns → our 4 blocks

Skill pattern **Hero + Testimonials + CTA** maps cleanly to our architecture:

| Our block | Hook                            | Adopt from skill                                                    | Reject from skill                           |
| --------- | ------------------------------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------- | ------------------------------------------- |
| Hero      | `data-marketing-home-hero`      | Full-bleed photo + scrim; sticky CTA; 32px+ display type on ≥1024px | Immersive full-screen JS; dark navy palette |
| Latest    | `data-marketing-home-latest`    | Card elevation, scroll-snap mobile, cover-first cards               | Feature grid with 6+ icons                  |
| Trust     | `data-marketing-home-trust`     | Logo + short tagline (real branding)                                | Fake review counts / star ratings           |
| Final CTA | `data-marketing-home-final-cta` | Repeat primary CTA after social proof                               | Second divergent CTA copy                   |

### Step 4 — Implement PR-4 (CSS-first)

See §7 file checklist. **Mobile-first:** write base rules at 375px, enhance at `640px` / `1024px`.

### Step 5 — Verify (fast path)

```bash
pnpm --filter @apps/marketing run lint
pnpm --filter @apps/marketing run test -- test/home-*.spec.ts test/guest-theme-stack.spec.ts
pnpm run guard:marketing-home-hooks
pnpm --filter @apps/marketing run test:smoke:home   # explicit YES for E2E
```

Manual: 375px RTL · no `overflow-x` on body · hero LCP ≤2.5s (manual Lighthouse) · urban `/` unchanged (minimal).

---

## 5. CP-SKILL — decision filter (mandatory after every skill run)

After Step 1–2, fill this table before writing code:

| Skill suggestion                       | Verdict     | Reason                                |
| -------------------------------------- | ----------- | ------------------------------------- |
| Colors `#1E3A5F` / Outfit fonts        | **REJECT**  | Conflicts LOCK §3.1                   |
| Pattern: Hero + Testimonials + CTA     | **ADOPT**   | Matches 4-block manifest              |
| Pattern: Scroll-Triggered Storytelling | **REJECT**  | Perf + hook stability                 |
| Style: Vibrant block-based             | **PARTIAL** | Large section gaps + scroll-snap only |
| UX: prefers-reduced-motion             | **ADOPT**   | Already required §12                  |
| UX: touch ≥44px, gap ≥8px              | **ADOPT**   | CTA + card taps                       |
| Immersive/interactive experience       | **REJECT**  | Client JS budget = 1 boundary max     |

**One-line rule:** _Layout and motion vocabulary from skill; brand tokens from MASTER only._

