## PR-mobile-gutter — footer + section spacing fix (2026-07-04)

**Symptom:** On mobile (375px), footer and landing sections looked «missing» or flush to screen edges — no horizontal breathing room.

**Root cause:** `denali-marketing.css` used `--space-10` / `--space-12` in `padding` shorthands, but guest design tokens only define `--space-1`…`6` and `--space-8`. Invalid `var()` values cause the **entire** shorthand to be dropped → computed `padding: 0`.

**Fix (CSS-only, shell block):**

| Token                      | Value                                                                           |
| -------------------------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |
| `--space-10`               | `calc(var(--space-8) + var(--space-2))` → 3.5rem                                |
| `--space-12`               | `calc(var(--space-8) + var(--space-4))` → 4rem                                  |
| `--catalog-page-padding-x` | `max(var(--space-4), safe-area insets)` mobile; `max(var(--space-6), …)` ≥640px |

**Footer:** `padding-block-start: var(--space-10)` · `padding-block-end: max(var(--space-6), env(safe-area-inset-bottom))` · `padding-inline: var(--catalog-page-padding-x)`.

**Catalog main:** same gutter token + safe-area bottom on `/tours`.

**Verify:** DevTools → `footer[data-marketing-footer]` computed padding ≠ `0`; scroll to page bottom on `/` and `/tours` at 375px.

## PR-home-mobile-gutter-closure — landing `/` (2026-07-14)

**Symptom:** On mobile, landing sections felt misaligned vs header and `/tours` — carousels broke out to screen edges while titles stayed inset; gallery filmstrip had double horizontal padding.

**Root cause:** `main[data-marketing-home]` uses `padding: 0` (PR-15 cinematic hero). Horizontal gutters come from per-section rules, but carousel rows used `margin-inline: calc(-1 * var(--catalog-page-padding-x))` breakout (featured, latest, destinations, gallery filmstrip). Gallery `div[data-marketing-home-gallery-support]` added a **second** `padding-inline` inside an already-padded section.

**Fix (`33-pr-home-mobile-gutter-closure.css`, ≤767px):**

| Rule | Behavior |
| ---- | -------- |
| Tokens | `--catalog-page-padding-y: space-4`; tighter `--mkt-section-pad-y` / `--mkt-section-header-gap` on mobile |
| Sections | All non-hero sections: explicit `padding-inline: var(--catalog-page-padding-x)` |
| Carousels | Remove negative-margin breakout; scroll rows stay in-gutter (`margin/padding-inline: 0`) |
| Card widths | `--mkt-home-scroll-card-width: calc(100% - space-6)` — cards sized to padded section, not `85vw` viewport |
| Hero | `data-marketing-home-hero-layout` uses same `--catalog-page-padding-x` as shell header |
| Gallery | Filmstrip/support: no double padding; scroll buttons inset `space-2` from card edge |
| Footer | `padding-inline: max(--catalog-page-padding-x, safe-area insets)` |

**Verify:** 375px RTL — section headers, featured/latest cards, destinations row, and footer links share the same left/right inset as `[data-marketing-header-inner]`.

