## Phase 8.5 — evidence-based visual polish (2026-08-18)

**Mode:** LOCAL Denali marketing CSS + one overlay-Header scroll island. No new product, no catalog IA change, no fake program covers, Walk Hero unchanged.

Phase 8.4 scored the **complete** landing 7.4. Two **visible-design P2** issues were polishable without touching asset/architecture debt:

| Issue | Evidence | Fix |
| ----- | -------- | --- |
| Cool-gray smear | Destinations / Gallery / FAQ / Final CTA all computed `rgb(246, 247, 249)` because `background: var(--color-bg-page)` leaked platform `light.css` `#f6f7f9` | Pin **explicit Denali mist/white chapters** (do not restyle Final CTA card internals) |
| Overlay Header on white Programs | Fixed transparent overlay sat on the programs title | Overlay Header becomes a **mist running-head** after the Walk Hero exits (`data-marketing-header-scrolled`) |

### Section rhythm (after Why)

```text
Hero          photo
Programs      --color-bg-surface (#fff)
Destinations  --denali-mist-50   (#f4f7f4)   explicit; not --color-bg-page
Why           --color-bg-surface (#fff)
Gallery       --denali-mist-100  (#e8efe8)   deeper mist chapter
FAQ           --color-bg-surface (#fff)
Final CTA     --denali-mist-50   (section only; panel still forest-tint on white)
Footer        --denali-mist-50
```

### Overlay Header scrolled state

- Rest: Walk overlay stays transparent ink (`hero.css`).
- Scrolled: `[data-marketing-header-scrolled]` + LOCAL `home/header-overlay-scrolled.css`.
- Island: `MarketingHeaderOverlayScroll` in MarketingShell — no-ops unless overlay Header exists. Threshold = Walk Hero height minus Header height.
- Landing sections: `scroll-margin-block-start: var(--mkt-header-height)` so chapter titles are not eaten by the running-head on in-page jump.
- Ink stays `#1a1f24`. No dark glass, no Walk restyle.

### FA H1 (P2 bilingual gap, local only)

Vazirmatn stay. `font-weight: 800` + tighter tracking on FA Walk H1. No Calistoga-for-Persian. No layout change.

### Out of scope (8.4 buckets)

- Identical `fallback-tour-cover.webp` × 4 — **content/asset**. Do not invent CSS uniqueness.
- Catalog search/chip on Programs — **architecture**.
- Triple `/tours` verbs, empty alts, SHENSKI vs shenski, destination CTA row — P3 / copy.

